  "slug": "circadian-reveal-abaf",
  "summary": "Integrated transcriptomic, proteomic, and single-cell datasets are being mined with machine learning to prioritize candidate diagnostic genes and proteins.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is discovery-stage biomarker nomination from omics data using machine learning and network methods. Across the set, transcriptomic profiles (bulk and single-cell), serum or plasma proteomics, and eQTL-linked data are analyzed with classifiers such as LASSO, random forest, SVM-RFE, and Elastic Net, alongside WGCNA and immune deconvolution. Diseases span glioblastoma, sepsis, allergic rhinitis, Kawasaki disease, obstructive sleep apnoea, MASLD, ARDS, psoriasis, and ulcerative colitis. Distinctive methodological steps include in silico knockout with scTenifoldKnk to nominate SORT1 in septic shock CD16+ monocytes, and regression of CPTAC tumor proteomics against transcript levels to separate self-driven from interaction-driven proteins. The IRF1 ulcerative colitis analysis is explicitly hypothesis-generating, so its associations remain provisional. The items do not share a common mechanism; the common contribution is a multi-omics prioritization workflow.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-10-05"
}
